XAttack types:  The various attack types possible for an attack are listed 
X  below, with a brief explanation for each.
X
X  Attack
X   Type       Description
X  ------      -----------
X  Bite      - The monster will attempt to bite you.
X  Breath    - With this attack type, the monster will breathe at you, usually 
X              breathing a gas, liquid, fire, or the like.  The classical 
X              example of this is the fire breathing dragon (a red dragon in 
X              nethack and most fantasy role playing games). 
X  Butt      - The monster will head-butt you, much in the same way that a bull 
X              would, usually in order to bring a horn into play.
X  Claw      - The monster attacks using its claws.
X  Defensive - This attack type will only occur if you successfully attack 
X              (i.e. hit) the monster in question.  I.E. this is a retributive 
X              strike.
X  Engulf    - The monster will attempt to engulf you.  This can involve 
X              swallowing you whole, as a purple worm would do, or simply 
X              surrounding you, as a fog cloud would. 
X  Explode   - With this attack type, the monster will literally explode if you 
X              come within range of it, and the explosion does the damage.
X  Gaze      - The monster will look at you in order attack.  Usually you have 
X              to meet the monster's gaze in order for the attack to be 
X              successful. 
X  Hug       - With this attack type, the monster will use a crushing bear-like 
X              hug in order to incapacitate you as well as prevent you from 
X              running away. 
X  Kick      - The monster will kick you.  For example, a horse (if it were a 
X              nethack monster) would probably kick you.  Temple priest(ess)s 
X              also use kicking attacks. 
X  Magic     - The monster will use a magic spell to attack.
X  Spit      - The monster will spit at you, and if the liquid that is spat 
X              touches you, the attack is successful.  A prime example of this 
X              type of attack would be the spitting cobra. 
X  Sting     - The monster will attempt to sting you with a stinger.
X  Touch     - In order to successfully attack with this attack type, the 
X              monster need only touch you. 
X  Weapon    - The monster in question will use a weapon of some type in order 
X              to do the damage listed.  Thus, monsters with this attack type 
X              will always be generated with weapons.
X
XDamage:  Damage is listed in the format XdY.  In this format, X is the number 
X  of dice rolled to determine the damage, and Y is the number of faces on each 
X  die rolled.  Thus, if '1d6' were listed, it would mean that one six-sided 
X  die would be rolled to determine the damage, giving a possible range of 1-6.  
X  If '3d8' were listed, it would mean that three eight-sided dice would be 
X  rolled to determine the damage, giving a possible range of 3-24.  
X
X  Note: where "LEV" is listed (i.e. "LEVd4" or "(LEV+1)d4") then substitute 
X  the monster's level for "LEV."
X
X  Note that with some damage types, the damage indicated here will not be used 
X  for actual hit point damage to the character, but may be used (for example) 
X  to determine the length of paralyzation or blindness, etc. 
X
XDamage types:  The various damage types possible for an attack are listed 
X  below, with a brief explanation for each.  The default damage type (i.e. if 
X  no damage type is listed for the attack) is "Physical." 
X
X  Damage
X   Type           Description
X  ------          -----------
X  Acid          - The damage done in this case is via acid.  Thus, if you are 
X                  acid resistant (only certain monsters are), you would take 
X                  no damage. 
X  Amulet        - Monsters with this damage type (basically the Wizard of 
X                  Yendor only) will attempt to steal the Amulet of Yendor 
X                  (assuming you have it). 
X  Blind         - This damage type is used in conjuction with the engulf, 
X                  explode, and spit attack types.  With the engulf attack 
X                  type, normal damage is done, and you will be blinded until 
X                  you manage to kill the creature or are expelled from it.  
X                  With the explode attack type, you will be blinded for a 
X                  number of rounds equal to the listed damage, but no damage 
X                  will be taken.  For the spit attack type, you will take 
X                  normal damage and be blinded for 1-25 rounds. 
X  Cleric Spl    - Monsters with this damage type will cast a random cleric 
X                  spell, having random effects depending upon the spell cast.
X  Cold          - The damage is done via cold or freezing.  Thus, if you are 
X                  cold resistant, no damage will be done.  However, this type 
X                  of damage also has a chance of destroying potions. 
X  Con.          - Damage of this type has the possibility of being poisoned.  
X                  If the attack is poisoned, your character will lose 3 to 5 
X                  points of constitution in addition to the normal damage 
X                  taken. 
X  Confuse       - An attack doing damage of this type will confuse you for the 
X                  number of rounds that would normally be damage.  (i.e. if 
X                  1d6 is listed for damage, you would be confused for 1d6 
X                  rounds).  No normal damage is received, however.
X  Curse         - If an attack using this damage type succeeds, the attacking 
X                  monster will "steal" one of your intrinsics.
X  Decay         - This damage type, in addition to doing normal damage, has 
X                  the capability of decaying organic material.  Thus, it can 
X                  damage armor that is organic in nature (i.e. robes, leather 
X                  armor, etc.). 
X  Dex.          - Damage of this type has the possibility of being poisoned.  
X                  If the attack is poisoned, your character will lose 3 to 5 
X                  points of dexterity in addition to the normal damage taken. 
X  Digest        - This damage type occurs only in conjunction with the attack 
X                  type "Engulf."  Basically, once the monster has swallowed 
X                  you whole, any damage done if via digestion in the monster's 
X                  stomach. 
X  Disease       - In addition to the normal damage done, you also have a 
X                  chance of becoming sick and eventually dying of it.
X  Disint./Death - This type of attack will usually kill you outright.  
X                  However, if the attack is a disintegration beam and you are 
X                  wearing armor, your outermost layer of armor will be 
X                  destroyed instead. 
X  Drain Energy  - Damage of this type is done by draining the amount of damage 
X                  from your store of energy points instead of from hit points.
X  Drain Life    - Monsters doing this kind of damage have a chance of draining 
X                  an experience level from you in addition to the normal 
X                  damage done. 
X  Fire          - The damage is done via fire or heat.  Thus, if you are fire 
X                  resistant, no damage will be done.  This type of damage also 
X                  has a chance of catching scrolls and spellbooks on fire, and 
X                  causing potions to boil and burst. 
X  Heal          - This is probably the most unique of all the damage types, 
X                  and is basically reserved for nurses.  If you are wearing 
X                  any type of armor, or are wielding any weapon when this 
X                  damage type is done to you, normal damage will occur (unless 
X                  you are a healer, in which case you'll get a fun message).  
X                  If, however, you aren't wearing any armor, and are not 
X                  wielding any weapon, you will actually be healed by the 
X                  attack, and if already at maximum hit points, there is a 
X                  chance that your maximum will be increased by one point. 
X  Legs          - Monsters doing this type of damage attack and do damage 
X                  primarily to your legs.  Such damage can incapacitate you 
X                  and prevent you from walking or fighting, especially if 
X                  you're carrying a heavy load. 
X  Lycanthropy   - Monsters with this damage type have a chance of not only 
X                  doing normal damage, but also conferring lycanthropy upon 
X                  you.  If you catch lycanthropy (signified by the message, 
X                  "You feel feverish."), you will periodically change form 
X                  into a rat, jackal, or wolf, depending upon which type of 
X                  lycanthrope you got the disease from. 
X  Mag. Mis.     - Attacks with this damage type are made via magic missiles.  
X                  If you are magic resistant, no damage will be sustained.
X  Paralyze      - For most attack types, this kind of damage includes not only 
X                  the normal physical damage, but also the chance of being 
X                  paralyzed for a random time period.  However, for 
X                  "Defensive" attacks, no damage is done, and you will be 
X                  paralyzed for the number of rounds listed as damage. 
X  Petrify       - Monsters doing this type of damage have a chance of turning 
X                  you to stone.  Generally the stoning (as it's called) starts 
X                  with the limbs, and then proceeds to the rest of the body. 
X  Physical      - The damage done is physical in nature (i.e. a cut to the 
X                  torso, etc.).
X  Rust          - Damage of this type has the capability of rusting metal.  If 
X                  the attack type is defensive in nature, the weapon you used 
X                  to attack can rust.  Otherwise, any metal armor you might be 
X                  wearing can rust.
X  Seduce        - Monsters with this damage type will attempt to seduce you 
X                  and will steal as many of your items as possible while they 
X                  are seducing you.  Incubi/Succubi have slightly different 
X                  effects with this damage type, and can have effects ranging 
X                  from giving you experience to outright killing you.
X  Shock         - Damage of this type is done via electrical shock.  Thus, if 
X                  you are shock resistant, no damage will be done.  However, 
X                  this damage also has a chance of destroying wands and rings. 
X  Sleep         - If an attack doing sleep damage succeeds, there is a chance 
X                  that you will be put to sleep for a random time period in 
X                  addition to the normal damage.  Sleep resistance will 
X                  prevent you from being put to sleep, but you will still 
X                  sustain the normal damage. 
X  Slow          - Attacks doing damage of this type have the possibility of 
X                  not only doing normal damage, but also of slowing you down 
X                  to normal speed if you are moving at faster than normal 
X                  speed. 
X  Spell         - Monsters with this damage type will cast a random magic-user 
X                  spell, having varying effects depending upon the spell cast. 
X  Steal         - Monsters with this damage type will attempt to steal an item 
X                  from your inventory.
X  Steal $       - Monsters with this damage type will attempt to steal any 
X                  gold which you might have.
X  Stick         - If an attack doing damage of this type succeeds, in addition 
X                  to doing the normal damage, you will be unable to escape the 
X                  monster in the next round. 
X  Str.          - Damage of this type has the possibility of being poisoned.  
X                  If the attack is poisoned, your character will lose 3 to 5 
X                  points of strength in addition to the normal damage taken. 
X  Stun          - An attack doing damage of this type will stun you for the 
X                  number of rounds that would normally be damage.  (i.e. if 
X                  1d6 is listed for damage, you would be stunned for 1d6 
X                  rounds).  In addition to stunning you for this time period, 
X                  you will take damage equal to one-half of the time period 
X                  you are stunned.  (I.e., let's say the monster can do 1d6 
X                  damage.  Let's say it rolls a 4 for that 1d6.  Thus, you 
X                  would be stunned for 4 rounds, and take 2 hit points of 
X                  damage.)  The exception to all this is "Defensive" attacks, 
X                  where you will be stunned as per a normal stun attack, but 
X                  no physical damage is taken. 
X  Teleport      - Monsters doing damage of this type can, in addition to doing 
X                  normal damage, teleport you to another spot on the level.
X  Wrap          - This is a special damage type which is similar to "Stick."  
X                  However, this damage type is reserved for eels, and if 
X                  successful, in addition to keeping you from running away the 
X                  next round, they have a chance of pulling you into the water 
X                  and drowning you. 
X
